          "model": "composer-1.5",
          "content": "---\ntitle: Preview Design\ndescription: Visualize your model using the Preview Design component\nicon: 🖼️\norder: 4\n---\n\n## 🔍 From Logic to Look\n\nOnce you've done the following:\n\n1️⃣ **Placed your Bricks** – by defining **Pieces** (instances of your brick molds)  \n2️⃣ **Snapped them together** – by setting up **Connections** between their Connectors  \n3️⃣ **Organized the build** – by assembling them into a full **Design**\n\n🎉 It’s time to **see your LEGO model come to life**!\n\n---\n\nUp to now, we’ve been working behind the scenes 🛠️\nWe’ve been defining meaning, relationships, and structure — not just drawing shapes\n\nBut unlike regular Grasshopper workflows, compose doesn’t preview geometry automatically ⚠️ The visualization happens in a dedicated step 🎬 like revealing your finished LEGO model after following all the instructions\n\n## 🧩 Visualize the Design\n\nOnce your modular system is ready, it’s time to see it come together!  \nTo visualize the final assembly, compose uses the `Preview Design` component in Grasshopper\n\n🔌 **Connect these inputs to the `Preview Design` component**:\n\n- **🧱 Design**  \n  The complete structure — tells compose which Pieces are used and how they’re connected\n\n- **📦 Types**  \n  The brick molds used in the Design — including Connectors and logic for snapping\n\n- **🧊 Models**  \n  The geometry files (e.g. `.glb`) or `Objects` for each Type and Variant — the actual shape of each brick\n\n---\n\n🔍 Once connected, the `Preview Design` component renders your full modular creation:  \nbrick by brick, just like snapping together your final LEGO model on the table! 🧩\n\nHere’s what gets visualized:\n\n- 🧱 **Brick Placement**  \n  Every Piece is shown in its final position — exactly where your Design logic places it\n\n- 🧲 **Connector Connections**  \n  All **Connectors** are displayed — including their direction — so you can clearly see how Pieces are designed to snap together, and which ones are actually connected\n\n- 🔄 **Snapping Adjustments**  \n  Rotations, gaps, shifts, or tilts added during connection are shown — making alignment easy to check\n\n![📁 Preview Design](/assets/images/preview-design.png)\n![📁 Preview Design](/assets/images/preview-design-2-black.png)\n\n---\n\n✅ That’s it — you’ve built and visualized your first modular kit in Compose!  \nFrom mold to model, every part now fits where it belongs\n",
